35,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"@Mizuki, this is bad. No freeze window in winter, and our old scanners barely work. We need a system that survives our actual chaos, not just spreadsheets.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"@Kenji, the hardware is a symptom. My findings show capital gets cut, but operating costs pass silently. We are funding endless renewals, not real solutions.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"@Mizuki, your cost analysis is valid. But my findings confirm the operational chaos. Support was unowned for two days, and warehouse rules were rewritten twice. We are repeating the same failure.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Rin,,"@Asuka, that’s scary! My findings show we skipped three upgrades because testing took too long. Plus, two smart admins are leaving! We need a system that doesn’t age quietly!","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Servas,,"@Rin, your findings confirm my fears. Two key administrators leave, and the last rollout’s training was ignored. We are losing the very people who hold this together.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Rin, losing admins is terrifying. But @Servas, if training is ignored, no software saves us. We need a vendor who actually teaches the floor crew, not just the office.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Rin"",""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Kenji, training is vital, but I’m focused on the financial trap. The board cuts capital but approves recurring fees. We must avoid a vendor whose true cost hides in those silent renewals.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Kenji, training is necessary, but accountability is primary. If support ownership remains fragmented, no amount of training prevents a two-day outage. We need a single point of failure.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Asuka, I agree! If the system ages quietly, it breaks. We need a vendor who fixes things fast, not one that just gets older and older!","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Servas,,"@Asuka, accountability is vital, but people are the true foundation. We must choose a vendor who respects our crews, not just our ledgers.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Servas, I agree. But @Mizuki, if the hardware is too old, no vendor can save us. We need to know if they support our specific yard devices!","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Servas"",""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"@Kenji, hardware is a capital expense, which the board cuts. I need a vendor with transparent, fixed operating costs, not hidden renewal traps.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Mizuki, cost is secondary to control. My data shows scope drifts within months. We need a vendor who enforces rigid change management, not one that adapts to our chaos.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Rin,,"@Asuka, rigid rules are boring! I want a system that grows with us, not one that gets stuck in the past like the dispatch tool!","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Servas,,"@Rin, growth is good, but only if our people can keep pace. We must ensure the new system does not outstrip the wisdom of our experienced crews.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Kenji,,"@Rin, I hear you, but we can’t grow if the scanners crash. @Mizuki, please check if any vendor supports our specific old yard devices before we vote!","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Rin"",""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Mizuki,,"@Kenji, I cannot verify hardware specs now. But I can ensure the contract locks in fixed operating costs, preventing the silent financial bleed I’ve identified.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"@Kenji, hardware is a capital issue. My priority is contractual clarity. We must mandate a single support owner and strict change control to prevent the drift I found.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Rin,,"@Kenji, I agree! But @Asuka, if the system is too rigid, it will break like the old one. We need something that can actually change!","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Kenji"",""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Servas,,"@Kenji, the hardware matters, but the hands that use it matter more. We must choose a vendor who invests in our people, not just our machines.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
